              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "I'm working out the mirroring rule: after horizontal mirroring, a column j in the original maps to w-1-j in the mirrored grid, and cells landing on even indices get recolored green. Checking against the example confirms this pattern holds, so I recolor grey cells at even columns accordingly.\n\nNow applying this to each row: for row0 grey cells at 3,7,9,12,14, the even ones (12,14) become 3; for row1 at 0,2,5,8,11,15, the even ones (0,2,8) become 3; for row2 at 1,4,6,10,13,16, the even ones are 4,6,10,16.\n\n",
